From 393091fff400222ff9a07c775e145a08a63e84f4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?St=C3=A9phane=20Payrard?= <cognominal@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 00:42:48 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 4/5] feat: hover help stands aside for the leader menu

While the leader or one of its menus waits for a key, the explainer is
not drawn: the menu is the next thing read, and two overlays on one
screen compete for the same glance. Moving the pointer under the menu
does not change the target, so the explainer comes back on the part it
left when the menu closes.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 docs/KEYBINDINGS.md        |  4 +++-
 e2e/tui/hover_help_test.go | 37 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++-
 internal/app/hover_help.go | 10 +++++++---
 3 files changed, 46 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)

diff --git a/docs/KEYBINDINGS.md b/docs/KEYBINDINGS.md
index 126eb80d8..3e1bb53b8 100644
--- a/docs/KEYBINDINGS.md
+++ b/docs/KEYBINDINGS.md
@@ -940,7 +940,9 @@ Hover help does not take the keyboard. Every other key, `esc` included, goes
 to the pane or to the open panel as usual, and so does a help key while a panel,
 hints mode or the leader has the keyboard. A click goes to what it lands on. A
 click on the explanation does nothing. The wheel scrolls the explanation when
-the pointer is over it.
+the pointer is over it. The explanation hides while the leader or one of its
+menus waits for a key, and comes back on the same part when the menu closes:
+moving the pointer under the menu does not change it.
 
 Bind the help keys in `[keybindings.help]`. The explanation's last line shows
 the keys you bound.
